A||||16||Fiero_24||How much HP can I get out of this rebuild?||||1||
Z||000000||Fiero_24||08-20-2001||05:58 PM||||Here is what I am having done to a V6.  <P>1. Throttle body and intake bored out.<BR>2. Performance kit from Fiero Store:<BR>TRW Power Forged pistons, Speed-pro   plasma moly ring set , Hi-volume oil pump, complete gasket and seal set, timing chain and sprockets, Crane valve springs, Crane cam and lifter set, Hi-Po steel retainers, all new oil galley and freeze plugs, cam , rod, and main bearings. <BR>3. Free flow cat, plus IRM muffler eliminator Y pipe<BR>4. Valves bowl ported plus Performance Valve Job<BR>5. Roller Rockers <BR>6. Power Pully Kit (Fiero Store)<BR>7. All new sensors and sending units, water pump, alternator and starter (I know the do not add extra HP, but they are new).<P>How much HP can I expect?  Does anyone have any ideas to add on to this kit?  Yes I could have gone with a V8 or 3.1, 3.4, ect..., but I want the stock looking V6 under the deck lid.  <P>Craig<P>------------------<BR> <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fiero_24" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/fiero_24</A> <BR>1987 GT||||reg||1
Z||000001||Phil||08-20-2001||06:19 PM||||You will probably equal a stock 3.4, which still looks exactly like the 2.8||||reg||1
Z||000002||Steve Normington||08-20-2001||06:39 PM||||Sortof OT, but...<P>I was watching one of the TNN car shows where they rebuild cars. They added new injectors and an adjustable fuel pressure regulator to a 94 F-body and got 4 hp more.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_wtf.gif"> IMS, they spend at least $500 for 4 hp.||||reg||1
Z||000003||pontiacs4me||08-21-2001||12:35 AM||||Those guys on horsepower tv have an unlimited amount of $$$ also.  Some of the things they do are just crazy and unacceptable for normal hot rodders to do.  I saw them put a full exhaust system on a camaro or something, headers back and added like 16 horse.  Cost like $900.  Id drop in a $400 nitrous system before I spent $900 on 16 horse.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Dave Gunsul||08-21-2001||12:57 AM||||Weren't you going to get headers or at least port the manifolds? If so, with the other mods as well you should end up with 190 HP which is more than a stock 3.4.<P>------------------<BR>Dave Gunsul<BR>N.I.F.E. member<BR>86 GT modified<BR>85 SE daily driver||||reg||1
Z||000005||Fierokid87||08-21-2001||01:13 AM||||Ok guys here is what Im doing.  The engine will have:<P>Borla cat back<BR>free flow cat<BR>sprint manifolds<BR>hyperutetic 9.1 pistons<BR>fully ballanced crank<BR>all rods matched to the lightest one<BR>blue printed<BR>stock cam<BR>stock valve train accept SI stainles perfromance valves<BR>3 angle valve grind<BR>decked block .20<BR>bored .30 over<BR>milled heads .20<BR>hypertech thermomaster chip and low tem fan switch<BR>cold air intake<BR>MSD 6A box, and GM MSD blaster coil<BR>factory red plug wires<P>Thats what Im having done so far.  Now it might change here and there.  Bt what do you guys think my hp gain would be or would it be next to non existant<P>Scott<P>------------------<BR><FONT COLOR="BLOODY"> Fierokid's  Web site <A HREF="http://www.angelfire.com/sports/sfiero" TARGET=_blank>http://www.angelfire.com/sports/sfiero</A> <P>AIM: Fierokid87<BR>ICQ: Fierokid</FONT><P>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sfiero.JPG">  <p>[This message has been edited by Fierokid87 (edited 08-21-2001).]||||reg||1
